Well the first time around I wrote a story, but this time I'll just post
the ascension statistics.  It was an interesting game in the sense that I
really didn't think it was going to go anywhere when I started, and
several stupid things happened like ...
     o  Deciding I was nearly invulnerable and deciding to quaff at 
        fountains and got my bag of holding cursed and pinned my 
        Valk to the floor...
     o  forgetting to switch weapons on disenchanters... those are
        rapidly becoming one of the more irritating critters
     o  killing lots of shopkeepers for a lot of money, and then deciding
        to read a spellbook without putting it all away... poof no
        gold
     o  putting on an uncursed helm to identify it at late mid-game, 
        finding out that it was a helm of opposite alignment, and finding
        out that this makes you lose all your nice bought protection --
        that was another expensive mistake
     o  wishing for a magic marker and writing a scroll of enchant armor
        in the castle and finding out that I had forgotten I hadn't
        discovered this scroll yet!  (first one was deep in Gehennom)

On the plus side, I never used an amulet of life-saving (had 4 at the end)
and was healthy and strong enough to wander around the Astral Plane (or 
at least one lobe of it) and make sure i picked up everything of interest
and occasionally whacking Pestilence when he decided to get up again. 
That was a nice feeling to see "Pestilence tries to flee!".  I thought
about trying to clear the Astral Plane of unfriendlies, but decided that I
haven't ascended enough times to be able to live with myself for a stupid
death because I got too bloodthirsty.

